WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.461
On most blockchains,

00:00:01.461 --> 00:00:03.339
anyone who knows an address can read its

00:00:03.339 --> 00:00:05.704
balance and every amount it paid.

00:00:05.704 --> 00:00:08.557
Nulo shows two balances for each token.

00:00:08.557 --> 00:00:09.983
Your private balance:

00:00:09.983 --> 00:00:11.513
only you can see it.

00:00:11.513 --> 00:00:12.939
Your public balance:

00:00:12.939 --> 00:00:13.983
anyone can see it,

00:00:13.983 --> 00:00:15.826
like a balance on Ethereum.

00:00:15.826 --> 00:00:17.078
Your private balance is a

00:00:17.078 --> 00:00:18.435
set of encrypted notes,

00:00:18.435 --> 00:00:20.522
like cash in sealed envelopes.

00:00:20.522 --> 00:00:22.087
The network keeps a fingerprint

00:00:22.087 --> 00:00:23.003
of each note,

00:00:23.003 --> 00:00:25.870
and a sealed copy only its owner can open.

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:28.583
Say you pay 3.5 from a note worth 5.

00:00:28.583 --> 00:00:31.713
Nulo spends that note and makes new ones:

00:00:31.713 --> 00:00:33.765
3.5 for the person you pay,

00:00:33.765 --> 00:00:36.026
and 1.5 change for you.

00:00:36.026 --> 00:00:37.243
In a private payment,

00:00:37.243 --> 00:00:39.643
the record shows that something was spent.

00:00:39.643 --> 00:00:41.417
It does not show which note,

00:00:41.417 --> 00:00:42.670
or how much.

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:43.991
Moving money to your public

00:00:43.991 --> 00:00:45.290
balance is your choice,

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:47.470
and the public side records the amount.

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:49.070
Nulo labels each balance,

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:50.948
so you always know which is which.
